      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Came across this problem aswell, in my case when my default audio device was switched to a \"non-renderable\" device that could not output audio itself.  (current pc uses a soundcard to output Dolby Digital Live over SPDIF, the moment DDL is activated the (stereo) SPDIF output is blocked by the driver as it will send an encoded bitstream through it originating from another listed audio device that windows sees as a  5.1 Speaker output.\n\nSimilarly should windows end up selecting this device while VRC is running (like when Vive Wireless runs out of battery and removes  the vive's audio device) it will crash the game",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-01-25T23:49:00.245Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "If you launch vrchat without any audio plugged in such as speakers, headphones, headsets, etc the game will run at about 8 frames a second. Once something is plugged in, it immediately goes back to the normal framerate. If you unplug it while the game is running the framerate will still run at the normal speed, it's only if you launch the game with nothing plugged in that lags.\n\nVideo showing this happen:\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GM9EtVXPt_M\n\nOutput log from the video:\nhttps://pastebin.com/z38M6Wnc",
